language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ heterosquare: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A heterosquare of order n is an n by n square whose elements are distinct integers from 1 to n^2
$ such that the sums of the rows, columns and diagonals are all different.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `heterosquare.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/heterosquare.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `heterosquare_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py heterosquare.json
$   savilerow model.eprime heterosquare_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the order of the square (the number of rows and of columns)
given n : int
$ nn: the number of cells, n*n; the entries are the integers 1 to nn
letting nn = n * n
$ x[r,c]: the entry in row r, column c (1-based)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..nn)
$ sums[1..n]: the row sums; sums[n+1..2n]: the column sums; sums[2n+1]: the main diagonal sum; sums[2n+2]: the other diagonal sum
find sums : matrix indexed by [int(1..2*n+2)] of int(0..n*nn)

such that
$ the entries are distinct integers from 1 to n^2
allDiff([x[r,c] | r : int(1..n), c : int(1..n)]),
$ the sums of the rows
forAll r : int(1..n) . sums[r] = (sum c : int(1..n) . x[r,c]),
$ the sums of the columns
forAll c : int(1..n) . sums[n+c] = (sum r : int(1..n) . x[r,c]),
$ the sum of the main diagonal
sums[2*n+1] = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i,i]),
$ the sum of the other diagonal
sums[2*n+2] = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i,n+1-i]),
$ the sums of the rows, columns and diagonals are all different
allDiff(sums)
